# Agent-configuration namespaces (.air/ and .agents/) are left fully visible to Git
# by default. This includes the generated .claude/, .junie/, and .opencode/ adapters.
#
# Do NOT ignore the whole .air/ or .agents/ namespaces, nor their plan directories:
# both may contain durable, shareable project artifacts that are intended to be
# versioned (e.g. worktree setup, Docker environment, MCP configuration, and review
# prompts under .air/; Skills and other project-scoped agent configuration under
# .agents/). Air plan files may be useful project artifacts, and plan directories
# are explicitly designed to be editable/committable.
#
# .agents/ is the canonical source of truth. .claude/, .junie/, and .opencode/ hold
# GENERATED platform adapters rendered from it by
# cli/tool/generate_platform_adapters.dart. They are committed (not ignored) so a
# product repo receives a working adapter set on bootstrap and so drift is
# reviewable; never hand-edit them.
#
# The same applies at this repository's OWN ROOT: .agents/, .claude/, .junie/, and
# .opencode/ at the top level are generated too — the root .agents/ is a MIRROR of
# framework/templates/__brick__/.agents/, not a second source of truth. `--check`
# covers both roots and fails on any mismatch at either, so an ignored or
# hand-edited root copy would be invisible drift. Do not add ignore rules for any of
# them.
#
# Generated does not imply transient: do not add ignore rules for tool-owned
# namespaces or generated artifacts without concrete evidence about their lifecycle
# and repository value. Default to visibility/versionability when uncertain; ignore
# only paths demonstrated to be local/session-only and not useful for collaboration,
# provenance, replay, or review.

# Compiled CLI binaries produced by the documented build gate
# (`dart compile exe bin/framework.dart -o framework_cli`, run by CI at
# .github/workflows/ci.yml and documented in WORK_STATE.md). These are ~7.6 MB
# machine-local build outputs, not source: they are reproduced by the gate and
# carry no information the source does not. Scoped to exact filenames rather
# than a pattern, so nothing else is swept up.
cli/framework_cli
cli/framework_cli.exe
cli/bin/framework
cli/bin/framework.exe
